  "title": "CRYPTO and PROVIDE EEG Baseline Data",
  "description": "Baseline EEG recordings from Bangladeshi children collected as part of the CRYPTO and PROVIDE studies. The dataset includes a cohort of 36-month-old toddlers and a cohort of 6-month-old infants who watched screen savers for 2 minutes. It was used to examine the association between stunting and EEG-derived brain functional connectivity in children exposed to early adversity.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded for 2 minutes while children watched screen savers. Participants with IDs below 2000 belong to the 36-month-old toddler cohort, and IDs above 2000 belong to the 6-month-old infant cohort.",
